## 1. Definitions

1.1 **Licensor** means Adrian Lipa / Intention Lab, or any successor or assignee of the rights in the Licensed Materials.

1.2 **You** or **Licensee** means any individual or legal entity accessing, copying, using, modifying, reviewing, executing, or distributing the Licensed Materials.

1.3 **Licensed Materials** means the software, source code, object code, scripts, configuration files, documentation, architecture, protocols, algorithms, schemas, prompts, agent contracts, governance files, reports, examples, tests, benchmarks, outputs, traces, logs, manifests, diagrams, specifications, and accompanying materials provided with or derived from this project.

1.4 **Software** means the executable and non-executable code portions of the Licensed Materials.

1.5 **Non-Commercial Use** means use solely for personal study, private experimentation, academic review, public-interest research, reproducibility testing, or internal evaluation where the use is not intended for, directed toward, or reasonably connected to commercial advantage, monetary compensation, paid services, production use, revenue-generating activity, investor diligence, product development, service delivery, or organizational operational benefit.

1.6 **Commercial Use** means any use by or for a for-profit entity, any use intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation, and any internal or external use that supports revenue-generating activity. Commercial Use includes, without limitation, paid services, consulting, contracting, production deployment, Software-as-a-Service, hosted access, managed services, internal tooling for a business, embedding into commercial products, integration into proprietary platforms, investor or acquisition diligence, customer demonstrations, resale, sublicensing, or distribution to third parties for any such purpose.

1.7 **Academic/Public Institution** means an accredited university, college, public research institute, non-profit research organization, public-interest laboratory, or government/public sector entity acting solely for non-commercial research, teaching, audit, or public-interest evaluation.

1.8 **AI/ML Use** means any use of the Licensed Materials for, in connection with, or as input to training, fine-tuning, distillation, alignment, reinforcement learning, preference optimization, evaluation, benchmarking, ranking, red-teaming at scale, safety tuning, embedding, vectorization, retrieval augmentation, dataset creation, synthetic data generation, model improvement, agent policy learning, automated agent orchestration, or creation of any machine-learning-derived system, model, weights, adapter, dataset, index, representation, or artifact.

1.9 **Model Artifact** means any model weights, fine-tuned model, adapter, LoRA, embedding index, vector database, dataset, synthetic dataset, distilled representation, learned policy, prompt library, benchmark corpus, evaluation suite, feature representation, or machine-readable artifact derived from, trained on, evaluated against, or materially informed by the Licensed Materials.

1.10 **Production Use** means use in live, operational, customer-facing, user-facing, revenue-supporting, safety-relevant, compliance-relevant, infrastructure, decision-support, or organizational workflow environments, whether internal or external.

1.11 **Hosted Service** means providing access to the Licensed Materials or derivative functionality over a network, API, website, application, agent platform, managed service, SaaS product, cloud service, or similar service, whether paid or unpaid.

1.12 **Derivative Work** means any modification, adaptation, translation, transformation, extension, port, fork, integration, wrapper, rewrite, reimplementation, or other work based on, incorporating, or substantially derived from the Licensed Materials.

1.13 **Offensive Use** means use that directly or indirectly enables, targets, plans, executes, automates, or optimizes armed attack, kinetic or cyber offense, target acquisition or selection, weapon guidance, lethal autonomous systems, malware, intrusion, exfiltration, surveillance aimed at facilitating harm, coercive profiling, or other operations intended to harm people, systems, or civil infrastructure.

1.14 **Human-Directed Transient Analysis** means limited, user-initiated, temporary inspection of the Licensed Materials using a general-purpose tool or assistant solely to help a human understand, review, debug, summarize, or evaluate the Licensed Materials, provided that such use does not create, retain, export, train, fine-tune, distill, embed, index, or improve any Model Artifact and is not used for Commercial Use, Production Use, Hosted Service, or AI/ML Use.

