## 5. No AI Training, Model Development, Embeddings, or Machine Learning Use

5.1 AI/ML Use is prohibited unless You have a separate written license signed by the Licensor.

5.2 You may not use the Licensed Materials to train, fine-tune, distill, align, evaluate, benchmark, rank, improve, embed, vectorize, index, retrieve, augment, or otherwise develop any AI system, machine learning system, foundation model, language model, agentic system, code model, multimodal model, retrieval system, vector database, synthetic dataset, learned policy, model adapter, or Model Artifact.

5.3 This prohibition applies regardless of whether the use is commercial, non-commercial, academic, internal, experimental, research-oriented, public-interest, automated, manual, temporary, or exploratory, unless expressly authorized in writing by the Licensor.

5.4 You may not ingest the Licensed Materials into training pipelines, fine-tuning pipelines, evaluation harnesses, benchmark corpora, RAG systems, vector databases, embedding stores, automated code analysis systems, agent orchestration frameworks, dataset curation workflows, telemetry systems, or model-improvement processes.

5.5 Human-Directed Transient Analysis is permitted only to the extent expressly allowed by Section 1.14 and only when it does not result in AI/ML Use, Model Artifacts, retention for model improvement, commercial exploitation, or production integration.

5.6 If You operate or control an AI system, model provider, agent platform, dataset provider, search/retrieval service, cloud service, code intelligence service, or automated analysis platform, You must not process, ingest, store, index, train on, evaluate against, or derive Model Artifacts from the Licensed Materials without a separate written license from the Licensor.

